The packaged executables are byte-identical snapshots of original canonical
scripts/setup/setup.py and scripts/repository/enroll.py. The repository guide
copies docs/repository-enrollment.md unchanged. source-provenance.json records
these paths and SHA256 values. check-sync.py must pass for each selected source
against canonical bytes before building or publishing from this repository.

No third-party template, service, font, compiled binary or platform component is
bundled. Optional configuration packages retain their separate package ownership.
Installing or removing this package does not activate/remove user configuration,
enroll/disable a repository, or import/remove/local-sign a public key. Those
operations require an explicit operator invocation of the appropriate CLI.

Setup8 successor adds the original MIT configuration migration engine and explicit
launcher/private setup contract. No third-party module or template is bundled.
The accepted Setup7 code remains separately pinned and unchanged outside this
variant; only migration-owned status guidance is corrected in the Setup8 copy.
